\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Pareizrakst\uc0\u299 ba
\f1\b0 \
\pard\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Latvian spell checking for macOS.\
\pard\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 What this installs\
\pard\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 The spell-checking service
\f2\i Pareizrakstiba.service
\f1\i0 , which registers with macOS as a Latvian (lv_LV) spelling service and runs in the background.\
\pard\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Choose where to install\
\pard\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 In the Destination Select step, choose whether to install the service for all users of this computer or for yourself only. Installing for all users requires an administrator password, while installing for yourself only places the service in your home folder.\
Before installing, the installer stops any running instance of the spell-checking service in the selected destination and removes it (either
\f3\fs22 /Library/Services
\f1\fs24  or
\f3\fs22 ~/Library/Services
\f1\fs24 )\
If you think Pareizrakst\uc0\u299 ba is already installed but are unsure which installation location was used, you can check these directories or use
\f2\i Uninstall Pareizrakstiba
\f1\i0  included in this disk image.\
\pard\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Usage\
\pard\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 For usage instructions, see the project homepage:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\li720\fi-720\sl288\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://warp-lab.github.io/pareizrakstiba/"}}{\fldrslt https://warp-lab.github.io/pareizrakstiba/}}\
\pard\tx220\tx720\li720\fi-720\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/WARP-LAB/pareizrakstiba/"}}{\fldrslt https://github.com/WARP-LAB/pareizrakstiba/}}\
\pard\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Uninstall\
\pard\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 To remove Pareizrakst\uc0\u299 ba later, double-click
\f2\i Uninstall Pareizrakstiba
\f1\i0  in this disk image. The uninstaller checks whether Pareizrakst\uc0\u299 ba is installed and reports where it is located. It then stops the spell-checking service, removes it from either or both installation locations, and preserves your learned words.\
